			"notes": "Fixes on top of v0.4.1. Same requirements: **Petrolpark's Library 1.5.0+** and **JEI 19.39.0.370+**.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- **Vat gas extraction changes the amount of gas** (#5) — pumping gas out of a Vat delivered `c²/ρ` instead of `c` moles per unit, so a full transfer between two Vats came out as roughly `A³ / (3V²ρ²)`: less than you put in below ~580 mol (2×2×2 vat), more above it. The extracted stack now carries exactly the moles removed from the tank. Regression from 0.3.8.\n- **Server crash when a fluid network outlives one of its endpoints** — blowing up a pipe or tank next to a running pump (or Creative Pump) killed the server on the next tick with `Do not call getCapability on an invalid cache or from the invalidation listener!`. Create's capability-cache provider only ever sets its `invalid` flag from the invalidation listener, and NeoForge skips that listener in exactly the branch that leaves the cache permanently unqueryable; a mixin now retires such a provider on the first throw so the network drops the dead endpoint and rebuilds. Reported by z209.\n\n- **JEI example fluid for ion ingredients** (#7) — the mixture JEI cycles through for an electrolysis input showed the bare ion; a solution matching that example would not electrolyse, because the recipe also needs a counter-ion present. The example is now the ion in water with a charge-balancing counter-ion, as upstream shows it. Electrolysis itself was working; the iron recipe wants 0.3–0.5 M iron(III), the same value upstream has shipped since the September 2024 snapshot.\n\n## Tutorial datapacks (#6)\n\nThe six `destroy_*_tutorial_*_en.zip` files attached to v0.3.0 were built with backslash paths inside the archive, which Minecraft silently ignores — the packs enabled but loaded nothing. Rebuilt and re-attached here and on v0.3.0. One tutorial reaction (`06_uv_catalyzed`) was not charge-balanced and is now H₂ + Cl₂ → 2 HCl; the READMEs no longer reference a `/jei reload` command that does not exist."
		},
